Make key-based partition selection deterministic. The producer indexed the murmur2 hash into a partition list whose order came from a ``set``, and the underlying metadata dict was built in whatever order the broker reported partitions, so the same key could map to different partitions and break key ordering (issue #1127). Partitions are now sorted by id when a ``MetadataResponse`` is consumed, and ``ClusterMetadata`` gained ``ordered_partitions_for_topic()`` and ``ordered_available_partitions_for_topic()`` accessors returning them in that order. ``partitions_for_topic()`` and ``available_partitions_for_topic()`` keep returning sets as before.
